class AppBoundary extends React.Component{
 state={error:null,attempt:0};
 static getDerivedStateFromError(error){return {error};}
 componentDidCatch(error,info){console.error('Cricket Empire screen render failed:',error,info?.componentStack);}
 render(){if(this.state.error)return <SafeAreaView style={{flex:1,backgroundColor:'#071211',justifyContent:'center',padding:24}}><Text style={{color:'#F2F1E7',fontSize:24,fontWeight:'800',marginBottom:10}}>This screen hit a problem</Text><Text style={{color:'#A5B4AE',fontSize:15,lineHeight:22,marginBottom:20}}>Your career is saved. Return to the main menu and try again. Error details are recorded for troubleshooting.</Text><Text style={{color:'#D4B96F',fontSize:13,marginBottom:20}}>{String(this.state.error?.message||'Unknown screen error')}</Text><Pressable accessibilityRole="button" onPress={()=>this.setState(state=>({error:null,attempt:state.attempt+1}))} style={{backgroundColor:'#D4B96F',padding:14,borderRadius:8,alignSelf:'flex-start'}}><Text style={{color:'#15251E',fontWeight:'800'}}>Return to main menu</Text></Pressable></SafeAreaView>;return <AppScreen key={this.state.attempt}/>;}
}
